    "question": "Aplica RK-2 para y'-2ty+1=0, y₀=1, h=0.6. Calcula y₁.",
    "solution": "f(y,t)=2ty-1\n\n  k₁ = 0.6·f(1,0) = 0.6·(0-1) = -0.600\n  k₂ = 0.6·f(1+(-0.6), 0.6) = 0.6·(2·0.6·0.4-1) = 0.6·(-0.52) = -0.312\n\n  y₁ = 1 + (1/2)(-0.600+(-0.312)) = 1 - 0.456 = 0.544",
    "procedure": "k₂ usa y₀+k₁ y t₀+h como argumentos."
